    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1228">

                <pb facs="0997" n="881" xml:id="pg881"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2912.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American Consul at
                        Ciudad Juárez</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-26T23:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 26, 1912—11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>You will immediately, informally, and unofficially advise Campa that under no
                    circumstances must there be any firing into American territory, and admonish him
                    that any violation of this warning will almost certainly lead to consequences
                    which it is to the interest of all true Mexican patriots to avoid. You will
                    impress upon Campa the very great seriousness of the situation and the
                    much-to-be-deplored results which would follow his failure to heed this warning.
                    You will convey a like message officially to the commanding officer of the
                    Federal troops.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
